Scott's Proposition 5.3 states that an approximable mapping \(f:\mathbf{A}\to\mathbf{B}\) sends elements to elements; that \(f=g\) exactly when \(f(x)=g(x)\) for every element \(x\) of \(\mathbf{A}\); that \(f\subseteq g\) exactly when \(f(x)\subseteq g(x)\) for every such \(x\); that \(x\subseteq y\) in \(|\mathbf{A}|\) implies \(f(x)\subseteq f(y)\) in \(|\mathbf{B}|\); and that for consistent finite \(u\) and \(v\), the relation \(u\,f\,v\) holds exactly when the closure of \(v\) is contained in the image of the closure of \(u\), from which the other clauses are said to follow. `Le` defines one approximable mapping to lie below another when every related pair of finite sets for the first is related for the second. `rel_iff_closure_le` is clause (v): if the relation holds, a token of the closure of \(v\) is reached by monotonicity from reflexivity on \(u\) and entailment of that token, using that \(u\) is contained in its closure; conversely the inclusion puts \(v\) inside the image of that closure, so some finite subset of the closure is related to \(v\), and entailment of that subset from \(u\), reflexivity on \(v\), and monotonicity restore the relation. `le_iff_toElement_le` is clause (iii), sending a related witness from the smaller mapping to the larger one, and in the other direction moving the closure inclusion of (v) across the pointwise hypothesis by transitivity and returning through the converse of (v). `ext_iff_toElement` is clause (ii): equality of mappings rewrites one image into the other, and equal images give both orderings by (iii), so extensionality of the relation yields \(f=g\). `rel_iff_forall_singleton` adds the equivalence of \(u\,f\,v\) with \(u\,f\,\{X\}\) for every token \(X\) of \(v\), by monotonicity one way and by induction on \(v\), using the empty relation and closure under union on the right, the other way. `Proposition53` conjoins (ii), (iii), and (v) as `theorem_53`. `Basic` describes that package and places the image of an element and its monotonicity before the proposition. Clauses (ii), (iii), and (v) match the note, and the proofs of (iii) and (ii) do run through (v). Clause (i), that the image of an element is an element, and clause (iv), monotonicity on elements, are not proved in the imported glosses. **Theorem:** partial — (ii), (iii), and (v) are `theorem_53`, while (i) and (iv) are absent. **Proof:** partial — the closure bridge, the pointwise order, and extensionality are proved, and the element and monotonicity clauses Scott derives from (v) are not.
